From: Pass 29 audit session <arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: Make the Miri gate's failure reason readable (diagnostics only, no behaviour change)

The Safety-gate job has failed in every recorded run (40/40 on the audited lineage).
The step-level record is always the same and is the whole of the available evidence:

    1 success  Set up job
    2 success  Run actions/checkout@v4
    3 success  Install Miri
    4 failure  Miri on nros-core        <- "Process completed with exit code 1"
    5 skipped  Miri on nros-types

There is no NROS-authored annotation for it, and job logs are served from
`*.blob.core.windows.net`, which is not reachable from every environment. So the cause
cannot be decoded from outside CI.

Note that step 3 *succeeds*. That is in tension with F-25's premise (that
`rustup component add miri` fails because RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=stable outranks
`rustup default nightly`) -- if the component were unavailable, `cargo miri setup` in
that same step would have failed. F-25 has never actually been exercised either: the
branch whose run is titled "apply F-25 Miri toolchain fix" (arena/01a03242-nros @
dee4f028) contains no ci.yml change at all.

This patch changes no gate semantics. It adds one read-only toolchain probe and mirrors
the Miri failure reason into workflow-command annotations, which ride the API rather than
the blob host and can be read with:

    gh api repos/Abdus2023/NROS/check-runs/<job-id>/annotations

The probe answers the one question that decides the fix: if `cargo miri --version`
fails, this is toolchain resolution and F-25's approach is the right shape; if it
succeeds, the `Miri on nros-core` failure is a genuine Miri finding in nros-core's
`MaybeUninit` / `drop_in_place` / raw-pointer code and must be treated as a P0 soundness
bug, not a CI defect.

Apply with:  git apply docs/audit/F-29-ci-miri-diagnostics.patch
(Cannot be pushed from the audit sandbox: the app token lacks the `workflows` scope --
the same limitation that keeps F-20 and F-25 unapplied.)
---
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 9105d8f..aa8e44b 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -84,8 +84,45 @@ jobs:
           rustup default nightly
           rustup component add miri
           cargo miri setup
+      - name: Probe effective toolchain (F-29 diagnostics)
+        run: |
+          # F-29: the Miri gate has failed in every recorded run, and the only visible
+          # detail is "Process completed with exit code 1" on `Miri on nros-core` while
+          # `Install Miri` succeeds. Job logs live on a blob host that is not reachable
+          # from every environment, so print *and* annotate -- annotations ride the API
+          # and can be read with:
+          #   gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/check-runs/<job-id>/annotations
+          # This step settles the one question that decides the fix: is `cargo miri`
+          # resolvable at all? If it is not, the failure is toolchain resolution (F-25's
+          # hypothesis). If it is, the failure below is a genuine Miri finding in
+          # nros-core's unsafe code and must be treated as a P0 soundness bug.
+          echo "RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=${RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN:-<unset>}"
+          rustup show
+          cargo --version
+          rustc --version
+          if cargo miri --version; then
+            echo "::notice title=Miri toolchain::cargo-miri resolves; a failure below is a real finding"
+          else
+            echo "::error title=Miri toolchain::cargo-miri NOT resolvable - toolchain problem, not a code finding"
+          fi
       - name: Miri on nros-core
-        run: cargo miri test -p nros-core --lib
+        run: |
+          set +e
+          out=$(cargo miri test -p nros-core --lib 2>&1)
+          rc=$?
+          printf '%s\n' "$out"
+          if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then
+            # Mirror the reason into annotations so it is readable without the log blob.
+            printf '%s\n' "$out" \
+              | grep -E "Undefined Behavior|error(\[|:)|panicked|no such command|not available for|MIRIFLAGS" \
+              | head -40 \
+              | while IFS= read -r line; do
+                  esc=$(printf '%s' "$line" | sed -e 's/%/%25/g' -e 's/\r/%0D/g')
+                  printf '::error title=Miri nros-core::%s\n' "$esc"
+                done
+            printf '::error title=Miri nros-core::exit code %s\n' "$rc"
+          fi
+          exit "$rc"
       - name: Miri on nros-types
         run: cargo miri test -p nros-types --lib
 
